      "observation": "16 bytes: earliest then latest double, static and instance IO variants identical. Default/reinitialize (+Infinity,-Infinity); ALL_TIMES (-Infinity,+Infinity), mutable object behind final reference. Copy and explicit-bound constructors; Coord[] constructor null yields default but nonnull empty accesses element zero. affect methods extend by strict comparisons; setters do not normalize or validate. Border true selects earliest. isTimeOrdered earliest<=latest; covers encloses inclusively; overlaps earliest<=other.latest and other.earliest<=latest; disjoints strict separation; contains closed, WithinLeft [start,end), WithinRight (start,end]. Typed equals compares endpoints, not equals(Object). remove only when corresponding left or right endpoints exactly coincide, adjusts one bound and returns true, no general interval subtraction or containment check. Intersection returns max starts/min ends if overlapping else null, duration clamps nonpositive to zero; duration getter unbounded difference. setZeroDuration sets both. toString doubles, short string float casts. main compares comparator object identity/equality and prints; not executed. Synthetic accessors expose private endpoints to comparators; static initialization creates four singleton comparators and ALL_TIMES. Formulas stated for ordered non-NaN intervals; no finite/NaN validation."
